Add GBARECOMP_CAPTURE: per-frame and per-line records for differential tests.

Comparing gbarecomp with another emulator, or two gbarecomp backends, needs
the machine state at one well-defined point of every frame. Headless runs
have no per-frame record (GBARECOMP_FRAMEDUMP_DIR works only in the windowed
loop, runtime.cpp:4217), nothing samples the state each scanline is rendered
with, and the MMIO write ring is fixed at 262,144 entries (gba_io.h:59): about
2,500 frames of a typical game, and 8 frames when an interpreter bridge spins
in BIOS IntrWait (about 30,000 IO writes per frame).

All of this is observation only, and off unless GBARECOMP_CAPTURE is set:

- src/runtime/frame_capture.{h,cpp}. At VBlank start, after the framebuffer
  latch and before the VBlank-timed DMA, the VBlank input hook and the VBlank
  IRQ, one TSV record per frame: CRC-32 of the 240x160 frame as BGR555,
  CRC-32 of the frame's line records, DISPCNT, configured EWRAM/IWRAM values
  and region hashes (with masked sub-ranges), the bytes the CPU and DMA wrote
  to FIFO A and B, the IO-register and HALTCNT writes since the previous
  record, the master clock, and the instructions the interpreter bridge ran.
  Before each visible line is rendered: its video registers (with masks for
  unused bits), palette[0] and CRC-32s of OAM, palette and BG/OBJ VRAM. Full
  line records, FIFO bytes and raw frames for requested frame ranges. A file
  sink, or stdout with a "[capture] " prefix for the browser console. Records
  are numbered frame_count() + 1, the count a VBlank-counting emulator such
  as mGBA has reached at that VBlank. The header comment lists the variables
  and the format.
- gba_io: gba_set_io_write_tap(), a tap on the MMIO ring's commit path, and
  GBARECOMP_MMIO_CAP_RING=<entries> to size the ring.
- self_heal: self_heal_bridge_steps(), the bridged-instruction count as the
  bridge runs (self_heal_interpreted_insns() grows only when a bridge
  returns, so a bridge spanning many frames shows in none of them).

With the capture off, the cost is a predictable branch per scanline, per
VBlank and per IO write.

Tested on macOS arm64 (Apple clang), plus an Emscripten 6.0.10 build of the
runtime, on a commercial ROM (Moto Racer Advance) with the retail BIOS:
- gbarecomp's 52 tests pass.
- Capture unset: runs of 240, 300, 320, 600 and 1,000 frames end on the same
  final line and coverage banner, with byte-identical --dump-png output, as
  the unpatched build, both recompiled and with GBARECOMP_FORCE_INTERP=1.
  Capture on: the same again, and two runs give byte-identical captures.
- The stdout sink prints the same records as the file sink.
- Over 66 frames (2.1 million IO writes), io_writes and halt_writes equal the
  per-frame counts of GBARECOMP_MMIO_DUMP with GBARECOMP_MMIO_CAP_RING=2097152.
- Against an independent implementation of the same records on mGBA 0.10.5,
  over a 3,000-frame boot: memory fields and FIFO bytes are equal on every
  frame, and line state on all but 18 frames, each a known difference of
  register-write timing or of an uninitialized register.

